              "text": "You are reviewing a rendered academic paper PDF for visual quality. The paper is for EMNLP 2026 ARR submission (double-column format, main body ≤8 pages).\n\nRead each of these PNG images and report your findings:\n1. /home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_11/projects/phase-gated-compound-sparse/artifacts/_project/paper/_pdf_images/main_p14.png\n2. /home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_11/projects/phase-gated-compound-sparse/artifacts/_project/paper/_pdf_images/main_p15.png\n3. /home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_11/projects/phase-gated-compound-sparse/artifacts/_project/paper/_pdf_images/main_p16.png\n4. /home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_11/projects/phase-gated-compound-sparse/artifacts/_project/paper/_pdf_images/main_p17.png\n\nFor each page, check and report:\n- Page layout: is it double-column? Do margins look correct for ACL/EMNLP format?\n- Any figures present? Are they rendered correctly, clear resolution, readable text? What figure numbers?\n- Any tables present? Are they rendered correctly, no overflow? What table numbers?\n- Any \"??\" unresolved references, \"[citation]\" placeholders, or \"Figure ??\" issues?\n- Any overfull hbox (text running into margins)?\n- Any large blank spaces?\n- What appendix sections appear on each page?\n- Does the paper end cleanly on the last page or is there excessive whitespace?\n\nReport findings concisely per page. Flag any issues as Critical/Warning/Minor."
